ey configuration is similar in both platforms.\", 'trans_template': 'ip address 172.16.1.1 255.255.255.0'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'tunnel source GigabitEthernet1/0/0', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'tunnel source GigabitEthernet1/0/0', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Based on the Juniper configuration provided, I'll translate one of the commands to Cisco IOS equivalent. Let's translate the GRE tunnel interface configuration:\\n\\n##\\ninterface Tunnel0\\n ip address 172.16.1.1 255.255.255.0\\n tunnel source GigabitEthernet1/0/0\\n tunnel mode gre ip\\n tunnel key 0\\n##\\n\\nThis translation corresponds to the Juniper commands:\\n```\\nset interfaces gr-0/0/0 unit 0 family inet address 172.16.1.1/24\\nset interfaces gr-0/0/0 unit 0 tunnel source ge-1/0/0.0\\nset interfaces gr-0/0/0 unit 0 tunnel encapsulation gre\\nset interfaces gr-0/0/0 unit 0 tunnel key 0\\n```\\n\\nNote: In Cisco, tunnel interfaces are named Tunnel followed by a number (not gr-0/0/0), and the tunnel mode is specified explicitly. The tunnel key configuration is similar in both platforms.\", 'trans_template': 'tunnel source GigabitEthernet1/0/0'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'tunnel mode gre ip', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'tunnel mode gre ip', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Based on the Juniper configuration provided, I'll translate one of the commands to Cisco IOS equivalent. Let's translate the GRE tunnel interface configuration:\\n\\n##\\ninterface Tunnel0\\n ip address 172.16.1.1 255.255.255.0\\n tunnel source GigabitEthernet1/0/0\\n tunnel mode gre ip\\n tunnel key 0\\n##\\n\\nThis translation corresponds to the Juniper commands:\\n```\\nset interfaces gr-0/0/0 unit 0 family inet address 172.16.1.1/24\\nset interfaces gr-0/0/0 unit 0 tunnel source ge-1/0/0.0\\nset interfaces gr-0/0/0 unit 0 tunnel encapsulation gre\\nset interfaces gr-0/0/0 unit 0 tunnel key 0\\n```\\n\\nNote: In Cisco, tunnel interfaces are named Tunnel followed by a number (not gr-0/0/0), an